  "body": "## What changed\n\n- The new module `crates/motion/src/wire_edm/rounds.rs` finds the facet vertices of a meshed round.\n- A vertex is a facet when it turns 30° or less. Its circle must have a radius of the kerf offset or more, and a chord sag of 0.02 mm or less. A neighbour must be a facet of the same circle.\n- The cover law in `laws.rs` gives each facet vertex its exact mitre excess, `k (1 / cos(θ/2) - 1)`. The allowance fades linearly along each chord.\n- All other vertices keep the strict `COVER_TOL` (2 µm). The refusal text does not change.\n- The decision is in `docs/decisions/3208-wire-facet-rounds.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe model mesh draws an r0.25 fillet in four 22.5° chords. The wire path is the polygon offset of these chords. At each facet vertex, the path stands `k / cos(11.25°)` off the profile. For the 0.25 wire (`k` = 0.162 mm), this is 3.2 µm past the offset. `COVER_TOL` absorbs only about 15° facets. Thus the law refused a legal radius.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew file `crates/motion/src/wire_edm/facet_tests.rs`, wire 0.25 mm, gap 0.037 mm (`k` = 0.162 mm):\n\n- `a_meshed_fillet_over_the_minimum_is_cut`: r0.25 in 4 and 3 facets, r0.5, r0.165 and r0.25 in 30 facets pass. On unchanged code it failed with the issue's text: \"near X4.927 Y4.927 ... would leave 0.0032 mm standing\".\n- `a_meshed_fillet_under_the_minimum_and_a_sharp_corner_stay_refused`: r0.15, r0.1, r0.155 and a sharp square stay refused.\n- `a_lone_kink_between_long_sides_stays_refused`: a single 22.5° kink stays refused.\n- `a_drawn_polygon_with_facet_sized_turns_stays_refused`: a 16-sided R5 opening stays refused (sag guard).\n- `a_short_notch_with_one_facet_sized_turn_stays_refused`: a short V notch stays refused (run guard).\n- `a_round_in_facets_past_the_turn_cap_stays_refused`: an r0.25 octagon hole stays refused (turn cap).\n\nMutation results (each guard removed, then restored):\n\n- `laws.rs` from upstream/main: `a_meshed_fillet_over_the_minimum_is_cut` red.\n- No `r >= k`: `..._under_the_minimum_and_a_sharp_corner_stay_refused` red.\n- No sag cap: `a_drawn_polygon_with_facet_sized_turns_stays_refused` red.\n- No run check: `a_short_notch_with_one_facet_sized_turn_stays_refused` red.\n- No turn cap: `a_round_in_facets_past_the_turn_cap_stays_refused` red.\n- Restored: all 6 green.\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` green on the final head (motion lib, wire_fans, app golden_cl and all app wire suites). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The heavy lanes (`cargo xtask gate heavy`) did not run. They must run before the PR is flagged ready.\n- The issue's real STEP parts (EDM-T1..T3) did not run through MCP. The test uses a synthetic 10 mm square with the same corner spot.\n- The path is still the offset of the chords. Against the true arc, it leaves the chord sag (about 5 µm for r0.25 in 22.5° chords) at mid-chord. This was already true before this change. The mesh resolution sets it.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. PR #3058 changes `wire_edm/open.rs` and `wire_edm/tabs.rs` only.\n\nChangelog: The wire corner check accepts a meshed fillet at or above the minimum inside radius; it no longer refuses a legal r0.25 round because of its mesh chords.\n\nFixes #3208\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
